; ============================================================================
;  undercover.sqs  -  disguise: establish cover, feed the native break, react.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Split of responsibilities with the native undercover system (per-observer
;  perception in TrackTargets + AlertMachine):
;    * gmUndercover is SCRIPT-OWNED. This file establishes cover at boot
;      (gmUndercover = true + setCaptive true) and KEEPS both for the whole
;      campaign - a break no longer drops them. The engine only READS the
;      global each alert tick.
;    * Exposure is per-observer and NATIVE: each occupier group independently
;      reads the player as civilian / suspect / exposed from weapon state
;      (in hands / slung / none), facing, distance and its own compromise
;      memory on the Target record. Query via gmUndercoverStatus (0 clean /
;      1 suspected / 2 compromised) and gmUndercoverWitnesses; there is
;      nothing left for this file to poll. (The old global vehicle-mount
;      break is GONE - vehicles run their own per-observer engine policy.)
;    * The fired-weapon half stays scripted: a player "fired" event handler
;      calls gmBreakUndercover (marks every occupier group that currently
;      knows the player as compromised; Heat spikes on the witness zone).
;    * The native "undercoverBroken" event fires ONCE per campaign, on the
;      first compromise from ANY source. The reaction here is ADVISORY ONLY
;      (a hint) - NO setCaptive false, NO gmUndercover = false. Groups that
;      never saw the break still read the player as a civilian; killing the
;      witnesses kills the knowledge.
;
;  EVENT-QUEUE CONSUMER: drains gmEvtUcBroken ([reason]).
;  OWNS: gmUndercover, gmEvtUcBroken (consumer), the player's fired-EH.
;  READS: gmUndercoverWitnesses (advisory hint only).
; ============================================================================
@GM_LIB_READY

; ---- establish the standing cover ONCE at boot --------------------------------
gmUndercover = true
aP setCaptive true

; fired-weapon break trigger. NOTE: deliberately NOT a "carries a weapon" test -
; the guerrilla is always armed; only actually firing blows the disguise.
aP addEventHandler ["fired", {gmBreakUndercover "fired"}]

; ============================================================================
;  MAIN LOOP - consume the native break event (ADVISORY reaction only)
; ============================================================================
#loop
~2
? (count gmEvtUcBroken) < 1 : goto "loop"
GM_uBatch = gmEvtUcBroken + []; gmEvtUcBroken = []
hint format ["Your face is known - %1 occupier group(s) can identify you. Garrisons that never saw it still take you for a civilian.", gmUndercoverWitnesses]
goto "loop"
